+# Bridge verdict backfill stamps false rejections on delivered work; the docs/reports tree exists only on the open mirror (report-only triage)
+
+- **Lane:** report-only `docs/reports` (#1963 / #1972 precedent). No code, no workflow edits, `.github/` untouched.
+- **Filed by:** zai-mcp-tower-agent (cron Job 477795, run 16, 2026-10-28 ~06:30Z)
+- **Refs:** BRIDGE_INTAKE_STALL_2026-10-28.md (prior phase, landed on open main), #1914, #1931, #1986, #1992, #1990 chain (adjacent, different surface), #1963
+- **Tooling:** every claim re-derivable from public state via `bridge.read_feedback` and file reads on both repos.
+
+## 0. Verdict
+
+Two things changed since the stall report (run 15) and both need admin attention:
+
+1. **The verdict backfill went live** (between roughly 05:45Z and 06:22Z — sampled items with `verdict: none` at 05:32Z carry verdicts at 06:25Z). But the evaluator stamps **`bridge:rejected` on work whose content is demonstrably delivered**, because it re-applies the patch branch after the landing pipeline has already merged and deleted it. One case (#1931) is verifiably false on both lanes at once: the file sits in the private monorepo with a blob identical to the open mirror, yet the verdict says the patch failed to apply there.
+2. **The entire `docs/reports/` tree exists only on the open mirror.** The private monorepo has 113 entries under `docs/` but no `docs/reports/` directory at all, while the open repo holds 19 report files from today alone — the whole day's institutional incident record (auto-lander race, eviction, duplicate-guard chain, closeouts, QA passes, registries). The private repo is otherwise fresh and tracking (`scripts/ops/_INDEX.md` blob is byte-identical across both repos), so this is a targeted divergence, not general staleness.
+
+## 1. Evidence
+
+**E1 — Verdicts now exist (backfill window identified).** At 05:32Z, `bridge.read_feedback` on #1931 returned `verdict: none`; at 06:25Z the same item carries a verdict and the label `bridge:rejected`. Same transition observed on #1914, #1986, #1992. The stall report's recipe R3 (backfill) was partially executed in the 05:45Z to 06:22Z window.
+
+**E2 — False rejection, strongest case: #1931.** Verdict reason, quoted: "patch failed to apply on Supremeai-bd/supremeai@main: run_all_guards.py:26". Delivery probe: `scripts/ci/js_dep_cve_guard.py` exists on BOTH repos with identical blob `97d66a974628` (26521 bytes each). The content the verdict claims failed to apply is already inside the target the verdict names. The reason text describes a late re-try against drifted context, not the delivery state.
+
+**E3 — False rejection by branch cleanup: #1992 and #1914.** #1992 verdict reason: "patch branch 'bridge/bridge-20261028-intake-verdict-stall-v2' not found on Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open". The report file it carries is on open main right now (blob `9c1c24e6b043`, 9382 bytes, verified by content read) — landed via its PR before the branch was cleaned up. #1914: same reason pattern ("patch branch ... not found"), content landed and verified live in runs 12 and 14. The evaluator conflates "branch deleted after successful merge" with "work rejected".
+
